* INPUT :                                                              *
*   kmode      : parameter determining the type of the sink term       *
*                                                                      *
*                kmode = 1 => space dependent kappa(z) sink term       *
*                             reflective boundary condition at x = 1   *
*                                                                      *
*                NB! when using this mode be careful to input right    *
*                    values of alpha, beta and k_expo                  *
*                k_expo = 6, beta = 0 => kappa(x) = alpha /(x^6)       *
*                k_expo = 0           => kappa(x) = alpha*exp(-beta*x) *
*                                                                      *
*                kmode = 2 => delta-sink term (K = kappa*delta(x-1))   *
*                             reflective boundary condition at x = 1   *
*                                                                      *
*                always using limiting behaviour of R(s,x)*g(x) at     *
*                x -> infinity                                         *
*                                                                      *
*   gmode      : parameter determining the type of transformation      *
*                                                                      *
*                gmode = 1 => optimal transformation, g(x) = constant  *
*                             The programme calculates the transfor-   *
*                             mation between z and x for the selected  *
*                             potential.                               *
*                gmode = 2 => free diffusion transformation, z = 1/x   *
*                             The programme calculates g(x) for the    *
*                             selected potential.                      *
*                gmode = 3 => the transformation, z = 1/sqrt(x)        *
*                             The programme calculates g(x) for the    *
*                             selected potential.                      *
*                                                                      *
*   vmode      : parameter determining the type of potential used      *
*                                                                      *
*                vmode = 1 => V(x) = 0                                 *
*                vmode = 2 => V(x) = xc/x  (Coulomb potential)         *
*                vmode = 3 => V(x) = xc*exp(-(x-1)/x_DSL)/x            *
*                                      (screened Coulomb potential)    *
*                vmode = 4 => V(x) =                                   *
*                                (v0/2)*[tanh(inv_thick*(x-xmic)) - 1] *
*                                      (potential modelling micelles)  *
*                                                                      *
*   dmode      : parameter determining the type of the relative        *
*                diffusion constant, gamma(x) = D(x)/D                 *
*                                                                      *
*                dmode = 1 => gamma(x) = 1                             *
*                dmode = 2 => gamma(x) = gam1 + (1/2)(gam1-1)*         *
*                                       [tanh(inv_thick*(x-xmic)) - 1] *
*                                                                      *
*   xc         : the constant parameter in the Coulomb potential       *
*   x_DSL      : Debye's screening length                              *
*   xmic       : radius of micelle in units of d (distance of closest  *
*                approach)                                             *
*   inv_thick  : the inverse of the thickness (in units of d) of the   *
*                layer between micelle and solution.                   *
*   v0         : parameter used in potential expression when vmode = 4 *
*   gam1       : gam1 = D_solution/D_micelle.                          *
*                NOTE: for dmode = 2, D = D_micelle, where D is the    *
*                diffusion const. used in the dimensionless variables. *
*   k_recom    : the dimensionless constant in the sink-term           *
*   ks         : dimensionless constant in expression for the          *
*                scavenge term                                         *
*                if vmode = 4                                          *
*                 then  Ks(x) = ks*(1 - tanh(inv_thick*(x-xmic)) )/2   *
*                 else  Ks(x) = ks                                     *
*   alpha      : dimensionless constant in expression for kappa(x)     *
*   beta       : dimensionless constant in expression for kappa(x)     *
*   k_expo     : dimensionless constant in expression for kappa(x)     *
*   nop        : number of discretisation points in z.                 *
*                Note that nn >= 1/sqrt(qddD) to ensure an effective   *
*                mixing of the spin states.                            *
*   delta_g    : (g1-g2) the difference in g-factors                   *
*                NOTE that the internal parameter qddD is given as:    *
*                qddD = larmor-frequency-difference / 2                *
*                     = delta_g * B02ddD / 4                           *
*   B02ddD     : = (g1+g2)*beta_e*B0*d*d/(hbar*2*D) = 2*B0*d*d/D       *
*   addD       : a*d*d/D, where a is the hyperfine constant.           *
*   jzero      : J0*d*d/D                                              *
*   alpha_d    : rex/d                                                 *
*                The two last parameters are used in the expression    *
*                for the exchange interaction, J(x)                    *
*                J(x) = Jzero * exp( - alpha_d*(x-1) )                 *
*   fs         : singlet character [0,1] used to set up rho(t=0)       *
*                The programme always uses a spin density matrix       *
*                of the form:                                          *
*                rho(0) = rho(0)nucleus * rho(0)electrons              *
*                rho(0)nucleus = 1/2|a><a| + 1/2|b><b|                 *
*                rho(0)electrons = fs|S><S|                            *
*                      + 1/3*(1-fs)( |To><To| + |T-><T-| + |T+><T+| )  *
*                                                                      *
*   sigma      : the dimensionless version of the parameter intro-     *
*                duced by the Laplace transform.                       *
*                                                                      *
*   scanmode   : parameter determining which variable is varied        *
*                = 1 : (x0_scan)      R(sigma,x0)  versus x0           *
*                = 2 : (xc_scan)      R(sigma,x0)  versus xc           *
*                = 3 : (v0_scan)      R(sigma,x0)  versus v0           *
*                = 4 : (xmic_scan)    R(sigma,x0)  versus xmic         *
*                = 5 : (jzero_scan)   R(sigma,x0)  versus J0           *
*                = 6 : (delta_g_scan) R(sigma,x0)  versus delta_g      *
*                = 7 : (k_recom_scan) R(sigma,x0)  versus k_recom      *
*                = 8 : (ks_scan)      R(sigma,x0)  versus ks           *
*                = 9 : (alpha_scan)   R(sigma,x0)  versus alpha_d      *
*                = 10: (B02ddD_scan)  R(sigma,x0)  versus B02ddD       *
*                = 11: (addD_scan)    R(sigma,x0)  versus addD         *
*                = 12: (h_scan)       R(sigma,x0)  versus inv_thick    *
*		 = 13: (sigma_scan)   R(sigma,x0)  versus sigma        *
*                The programme can vary any of these variables either  *
*                linearly or logarithmically.                          *
*                Linear scan use :                                     *
*                abs(scmin) < abs(scmax) if they have the same sign    *
*                scmin < scmax           if they have opposite signs.  *
*                Logarithmic scan:                                     *
*                abs(scmin) < abs(scmax) and they MUST have same sign. *
*   scmin      : minimum value of variable except for scanmode = 1     *
*   scmax      : maximum value of variable except for scanmode = 1     *
*   sclog      : parameter determining the form of the scan            *
*                = 0  : var. varied linearly in step of scfac          *
*                = 1  : var. varied logarithmically in steps of scfac  *
*   scfac      : step size in scanning.                                *
*   x0         : value of the initial separation                       *
*                not used when scanmode = x0_scan                      *
*   also_2n    : parameter determining if 2n-calculation is also done  *
*                = 0 : only calculation with nop points                *
*                = 1 : calculation for both nop and 2*nop points       *
*                                                                      *
*   ALL PARAMETERS MUST ALWAYS BE GIVEN TO THE PROGRAM                 *
*   DESPITE THAT THEY ARE NOT ALL USED (unused values are arbitrary)   *
***********************************************************************)

